    "narrative": "The offensive engine for Ghost Ride the WHIP centers on the high-upside matchup against Andrew Abbott today. **Corbin Carroll** leads the charge with an elite 80.77 score; despite a platoon disadvantage against the lefty, his matchup against Abbott and the benefit of hitting second provides the highest ceiling on the roster. **Gabriel Moreno** also benefits significantly from the Abbott pairing, securing a 66.77 score behind a strong 0.372 xwOBA and a favorable third-spot placement in the order. Meanwhile, **Vinnie Pasquantino** remains a set-and-forget anchor, leveraging a plus matchup against Waguespack to deliver our highest non-Carroll score (76.21) by capitalizing on his right-handed platoon edge.\n\nWhile the core is set, we are navigating a few tactical concerns. **Henry Bolte** is our most efficient bottom-of-the-roster play today, projecting for a 60.79 score primarily because his lead-off spot against Javier offers premium R/R upside despite the veteran pitcher\u2019s presence. On the bubble, **Isaac Paredes** was the most difficult exclusion from the starting nine; his 45.78 score fell just short of our daily threshold, as the matchup against Basso suppressed his base projections enough to favor the higher-upside profiles of **Mickey Moniak** and **Jose Caballero**. We are keeping a close watch on **Jose Caballero** and **Mickey Moniak**, as their utility value is contingent on their specific order placement and the need to insulate against the risks posed by Griffin and Soriano, respectively.\n\nRisk management remains paramount, particularly regarding the lower-end scores of **Austin Riley** and **Josh Naylor**. Both face challenging left-handed starters in Drohan and Imanaga, resulting in sub-50 efficiency ratings that hover near our bench threshold. We are comfortable starting them to preserve positional coverage, but any late-inning defensive shifts could see their value evaporate. Ensure all lineups are finalized, as we are currently operating under historical order assumptions for **Henry Bolte** and **Travis Bazzana**. With **James Wood** confirmed on the IL, we continue to rely on the depth of our bench, including **Griffin Conine** and **Cole Young**, to rotate in should any of our starters experience mid-game weather delays or tactical substitutions.",
